      <activity id="96de81a8-ff09-585d-af4e-0a4afef061d0" activityNameId="688c90b4-ad0d-5a6f-80de-8b4a49aaf276" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Acetone cyanohydrin, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Acetone cyanohydrin, at plant
Data are from the Eco-profiles of the European plastics industry (PlasticsEurope). Not included are the values reported for: recyclable wastes, amount of air / N2 / O2 consumed, unspecified metal emission to air and to water, mercaptan emission to air, unspecified CFC/HCFC emission to air, dioxin to water. The amount of "sulphur (bonded)" is assumed to be included into the amount of raw oil.;
CAS number: 000075-86-5; 
Synonyms: 2-hydroxy-2-methylpro-panenitrile; 
UUID: 69fc38b9-c577-3cb3-b1d2-dd37d22c46df
Aggregated data for all processes from raw material extraction until delivery at plant
Location: 3 European plants (D, F, UK)
Technology: production from acetone and hydrogen cyanide by base-catalyzed reaction
Time period: time to which data refer
Production volume: 330 kt (1993)
Sampling: literature values based on company survey 
Extrapolations: no extrapolation
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_69fc38b9-c577-3cb3-b1d2-dd37d22c46df.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
